y, but these confounders do not survive the time-respecting, 600-unit-gap requirement.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "**Conclusion:** The chain dies at the first hop.\n\n- 1010 has exactly **one** event in the whole 19,200-unit window (step_02), a single out-edge 1010\u219266 (step_05), localized by bisection to t \u2208 [70268, 70517] (steps 07, 10, 12).\n- For a cascade, 66 must re-transmit within 600 units, i.e. by ~71117. In [70268, 71117] node 66 has only **1** event \u2014 the incoming one from 1010 itself (step_14). No onward forwarding exists in the relay window.\n- 883's only in-neighbours are 729, 1038, 1209 (step_08); none of them is 66, and none is reachable from 66 in the temporal budget. 883's single relevant event falls in [70718, 71117] (step_15) \u2014 temporally plausible but sourced from 729-type contacts, not from any 1010-descended chain (1038 and 1209 are entirely inactive around then, step_13).\n- Confounder controls: the window is busy (4318 events, 1794 active nodes, step_01) and 1010 sits near high-degree hubs 1688/1824 (step_09), so an *order-ignoring* path from 1010 to 883 does exist through the hub-dominated 4-hop closure (step_04). That static connectivity \u2014 and the hubs' popularity \u2014 is exactly what fails once time ordering and the 600-unit gap constraint are imposed.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_07174392\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1010, 883],\n  \"window\": [60917, 80117],\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"narrative\": \"Node 1010 emits a single event (1010->66) at t in [70268,70517]. Node 66 has no outgoing activity within the following 600 units (its only event in [70268,71117] is that incoming contact), so the potential cascade terminates at hop 1. Node 883's inbound contacts come only from 729/1038/1209, none of which lies on any 66-rooted temporal chain. A static, order-ignoring path from 1010 to 883 does exist via high-degree hubs (1688/1824/158), and the window is generally busy, but these confounders do not survive the time-respecting, 600-unit-gap requirement.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 39531, "total_output_tokens": 4715, "total_tokens": 44246, "total_latency_ms": 68291, "llm_calls": 7, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}